              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Sections partition a page into a content hierarchy. In AsciiDoc, sections are defined using section titles."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "== Level 1 Section Title\n\n=== Level 2 Section Title\n\n==== Level 3 Section Title\n\n===== Level 4 Section Title\n\n====== Level 5 Section Title\n\n== Another Level 1 Section Title"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Section title syntax"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When a page is converted to HTML, each section title becomes a heading element where the heading level matches the number of equals signs. For example, a level 1 section ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "=="
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") maps to an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "<h2>"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " HTML tag."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Section headings must be defined using the Atx-style (single line) that begins with one or more equals signs."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora does not recognize the legacy Setext-style (i.e., underlined) heading syntax once supported in AsciiDoc, nor does it recognize Asciidoctor’s Markdown-style heading syntax. If you don’t use the Atx-style syntax, xrefs in the page will not be resolved and other features of AsciiDoc will not be available."
              }
